			"Message": "chore(Deps/Tauri): Batch update Tauri ecosystem submodules\n\nAdvance 30 submodules within Land/Dependency/Tauri to their latest upstream revisions. This covers the core Tauri runtime, plugin suite (Authenticator, CLI, Dialog, FS, FSExtra, FSWatch, GlobalShortCut, HTTP, Log, Notification, OS, Positioner, Process, SQL, Shell, StrongHold, Updater, Upload, WebSocket), tooling (TauriAction, TauriDocs, Tao, Wry, TauriSearch, TauriToml), and auxiliary modules (Meetings, PluginsWorkspace, RFCs).\n\nKey changes integrated:\n- **Cleanup:** Remove stray `.DS_Store` from Meetings.\n- **Tests:** Refactor TauriSearch pattern guide fixtures to use lowercase `<rater>` tags with proper nesting.\n- **Docs:** Widespread normalization of HTML table indentation from spaces to tabs and self-closing void elements across plugin READMEs and autogenerated permission reference docs.\n\nThis keeps the Land editor's dependency tree aligned with upstream formatting conventions and improves documentation readability without altering semantic content.",
			"SHA": "25368630c5deabea522b15966536877c3e86d3e8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-31T15:47:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				176,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps): Advance Microsoft submodule and reformat README\n\nAdvance the Microsoft VS Code Editor dependency submodule from a7aa78d2 to 31036490 to integrate upstream Agent Host filesystem operations, Agent Host Protocol resource lifecycle improvements, multi-pane enhancements, session deduplication, BYOK retry fixes, and telemetry hardening.\n\nReformat README.md with self-closing HTML tags and proper table indentation to correct malformed markup in the dependency project showcase layout.\n\nNo source changes in the Land application — pure dependency sync and markup cleanup to align the Dependency directory with upstream VS Code improvements for remote agent connectivity, session lifecycle, and multi-pane UX.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "a1b8347589ec9afb134056d945da9e8f76b155e7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-26T15:09:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				176,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps/Editor): Advance Microsoft pointer for Sessions Grid, SSH passphrase auth, and worktree timeout hardening\n\nAdvance the Microsoft VS Code Editor dependency submodule from 126808a4 to a7aa78d2 to integrate upstream improvements across sessions UI, SSH remote agent host authentication, and worktree lifecycle reliability.\n\nKey upstream changes incorporated:\n- Sessions Grid: Introduce a grid-based multi-session view with composite bar actions, open-to-side support, and close buttons always visible, replacing the single-session chat panel layout for the Cocoon extension host UI.\n- SSH Passphrase Auth: Support encrypted private key passphrase prompts for SSH remote agent host connections, resolving IdentityAgent from SSH config and falling back to on-disk encrypted keys for remote Mountain-to-Cocoon agent connectivity.\n- Worktree Timeout Hardening: Raise git worktree timeout from 30s to 60s with definitive timeout detection and summarized stderr for thrown errors in the Cocoon extension host.\n- Agent Host Improvements: Add chat.agentHost.runWorktreeCreatedTasks setting (default off), normalize LF to CRLF in terminal tool output, restore X-button removal of SSH entries, fix duplicate command registration for agent-host-copilotcli.\n- Remote Session Resilience: Preserve unread state across remote host disconnect/reconnect cycles by caching sessions instead of reporting them as removed.\n- Bug Fixes: Decode percent-encoded image names in carousel, guard against invalid lines in quick fix provider, handle IPC log race on removed logger, exclude settings from issue reporter wizard.\n\nNo source changes in the Land application — pure submodule pointer update to keep the dependency tree aligned with upstream VS Code improvements for remote agent connectivity, session management, and worktree reliability.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "47a63f93a2e50e05749dd880044a96c503fcb0e1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-25T19:07:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				176,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps/Editor): Advance Microsoft pointer for changeset caching and BYOK fixes\n\nAdvance the Microsoft VS Code Editor dependency submodule from e0ba18e1 to 126808a4 to integrate upstream changeset lifecycle improvements, offline BYOK resilience, and session navigation.\n\nKey upstream changes incorporated:\n- AgentHost Changeset Caching: Implement proactive changeset state tracking in the agent host editing pipeline, including caching, eviction of stale changesets, and a releaseBranchChanges method. Restore sessions from changeset subscriptions more reliably.\n- BYOK State Fix: Correct offline BYOK state management to ensure custom API key providers retain configuration when network connectivity is lost, with proper state reconciliation on reconnect.\n- Sessions Link: Add a dedicated sessions link in the chat view for direct navigation to session management, improving user access to session history and configuration.\n\nNo source changes in the Land application — pure submodule pointer update to keep the dependency tree aligned with upstream VS Code improvements for agent editing reliability and credential persistence in air-gapped BYOK scenarios.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "e481e786b2fa116c335f71781f705932106f83ca"
		},
